{"title":"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">2011 CIMC Part A Problem 4</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">2011 CSMC Part A Problem 3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A die is a cube with its faces numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. One red die and one blue die are rolled. The sum of the numbers on the top face of each die is determined. What is the probability that this sum is a perfect square?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> represent getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> on the red die and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> on the blue die. For instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> was obtained on the red die and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> was obtained on the blue die. Listing all the possible pairs, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5e0b708fc819443ed3b15981cc6282f96e0692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (1, 5), (1, 6),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3d9f87362dcdfcfb8adf735517c54b48c6ade72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 1), (2, 2), (2, 3), (2, 4), (2, 5), (2, 6),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c06507cbe4642ffc2e5e709924acfad0c15af322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1), (3, 2), (3, 3), (3, 4), (3, 5), (3, 6),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/497f4428e4e356f37b0e27c487e309310090af37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 1), (4, 2), (4, 3), (4, 4), (4, 5), (4, 6),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa5659ac00b71ec48172d1192ad6b1e565c73c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 1), (5, 2), (5, 3), (5, 4), (5, 5), (5, 6),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/3182e1fca083f5d925fcbc57cf91a57c77de6bc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 1), (6, 2), (6, 3), (6, 4), (6, 5), (6, 6),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This can also be made easier by using a table with the specific values:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>By looking at all of the different sums and counting, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities in total and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> where the sum is a perfect square. The probability of getting a sum that is a perfect square with the two die rolls is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5cde6306d6af9d41ce9e786da08343d48f72ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{7}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Without_Listing_All_Possibilities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Without_Listing_All_Possibilities)\">Solution 2 (Without Listing All Possibilities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Without Listing All Possibilities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> options for each die roll, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897dd68f9e342665851f9e9b91b87a28d42fc7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 6 = 36$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> possibilities in total.\n</p><p>The maximum sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a55c0d4c675fd3aa3072351ee200a52d394565.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 6 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and the minimum sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349b6b8a00581fb06095c20113d8fa49f3f5cf9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />, so we only need to look for the perfect squares less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> but greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We can obtain a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the first roll and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the second or vice-versa or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on both rolls. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities where there's a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We can obtain a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the first roll and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the second and vice-versa or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the first roll and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the second and vice-versa. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities where there's a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d81853f2ad863952d547351d2e8747cbde12da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 4 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities where there the sum of the two rolls is a perfect square.\n</p><p>The probability that the sum is a perfect square is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5cde6306d6af9d41ce9e786da08343d48f72ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{7}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC\" title=\"2011 CIMC\">2011 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Intermediate_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Intermediate Competition\">CEMC Intermediate Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC\" title=\"2011 CSMC\">2011 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Intermediate_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Intermediate Competition\">CEMC Intermediate Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018054743\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 286/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 3173/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 383/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 